From: KnutMann <knutmann@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:52:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Keep a profile picture at the resolution that was asked
 for

Two faults, one of them ours.

The setting deciding whether to fetch a picture defaulted to the full resolution while the code
deciding what to fetch still defaulted to the thumbnail. An account that had never been told
otherwise therefore asked as though it wanted the full picture and downloaded the preview. Ours:
the commit that moved the defaults to full resolution moved three of the four.

The second is why changing the setting afterwards did nothing. WhatsApp identifies a picture by an
id which says nothing about its resolution, the thumbnail and the full picture of one photograph
carrying the same one. Sending it along gets "unchanged" back whatever is being asked for, so a
thumbnail fetched once stayed a thumbnail for as long as the person kept the photograph.

The resolution is now remembered beside the id, and the id is only offered while it still describes
what is wanted. Where it does not, the request goes out without one and the server answers with a
picture. A picture stored before this carries no such note, which counts as a mismatch, so the
first connection after this refetches those once and is quiet again afterwards.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 glue/presence.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 profile.go      |  5 ++++-
 2 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/glue/presence.c b/glue/presence.c
index d381ce7..f5874a0 100644
--- a/glue/presence.c
+++ b/glue/presence.c
@@ -29,6 +29,34 @@ gowhatsapp_handle_presence(PurpleAccount *account, char *remoteJid, char online,
     }
 }
 
+/*
+ * Which resolution a stored picture was fetched at, and whether that is still the wanted one.
+ *
+ * WhatsApp identifies a profile picture by an id which says nothing about its resolution: the
+ * thumbnail and the full picture of the same photograph carry the same one. Sending that id along
+ * with a request therefore gets "unchanged" back whichever resolution is being asked for, so a
+ * thumbnail fetched once would stay a thumbnail for as long as the person keeps the photograph,
+ * no matter what the setting is changed to afterwards.
+ *
+ * Remembering what was fetched settles it. The id is only offered while it still describes what is
+ * wanted; where it does not, the request goes out without one and the server answers with a
+ * picture rather than with "unchanged".
+ *
+ * A picture stored before this was written carries no note of its resolution, which counts as a
+ * mismatch, so the first connection after this change refetches those once and is then quiet again.
+ */
+static void gowhatsapp_remember_picture_type(PurpleAccount *account, PurpleBlistNode *node)
+{
+    purple_blist_node_set_string(node, "picture_type",
+        purple_account_get_string(account, GOWHATSAPP_ICONS_OPTION, GOWHATSAPP_ICONS_CHOICE_ORIGINAL));
+}
+
+static gboolean gowhatsapp_picture_type_still_wanted(PurpleAccount *account, PurpleBlistNode *node)
+{
